<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leonard Calvert</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1606">1606</a>–<a href="/years/1647">1647</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leonard Calvert was the first proprietary governor of the Province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maryland">Maryland</a>, the younger brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cecil-calvert">Cecil Calvert, 2nd Baron Baltimore</a>. In 1634 he led the first settlers aboard the Ark and the Dove to St Mary's City on the lower Potomac. He governed the colony, a refuge for English Catholics, through Indian diplomacy and the disorders of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-civil-war">English Civil War</a> until his death in 1647.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leonard-calvert.jpg" alt="Leonard Calvert" width="320" height="447" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jacob van Oost / Jacob van Oost the Younger · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leonard_Calvert,_by_Jacob_Van_Oost_I_or_II_(1640).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
